    log(`${tag} review passed (${reviewFile})`)
  } else {
    log(`${tag} review skipped (diff < 80 lines, checks pass)`)
  }

  const integ = await locked(() => agent(`You integrate one finished litecode run of the Frame Job duplicate-code audit onto main. Issue #${it.n}. Lane worktree W=${L.path}, branch ${L.branch}. Handoff dir H=${H}. Main checkout M=${MAIN} (other sessions may use it: only ever run the git/make/gh commands below there).

Do these steps in order; run every command with absolute paths.
1. Read H/04-impl-notes.md, ${reviewFile ? 'H/' + reviewFile + ' and every H/06-fix-notes-*.md, ' : ''}and H/${specRef}. Collect (a) every "CLAUDE.md edits owed" item (spec and notes) and (b) any review NIT that is a one-line wording/doc fix. Apply (a) in W's CLAUDE.md / app/CLAUDE.md / core/CLAUDE.md in the file's own style (wrapped near 80 columns, rulebook prose, no status or history paragraphs), and (b) where cheap. Don't change code behaviour.
2. In W: \`git -C W status --porcelain\`; every change there is this issue's. Stage them explicitly (never FrameJob.xcodeproj, never tools/proof/work/, never tools/proof/media/), and commit on ${L.branch}. Message: a one-line subject saying what changed, ending "(#${it.n})"; a short body: what changed, "Verified:" (the checks from 04-checks.txt that passed, incl. any Release run), "Owed:" (or "Owed: nothing"); last line exactly: Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>. Do not write "Closes #".
3. \`git -C W rebase main\`. On conflicts: resolve them (appended sections such as tools/proof/README.md, CLAUDE.md map entries, spec index rows and Lines cells: keep both sides and fix counts; code: keep both intents), \`git -C W add\` the files, \`GIT_EDITOR=true git -C W rebase --continue\`. If you cannot resolve a conflict with confidence: \`git -C W rebase --abort\` and return conflict-unresolved naming the files.
4. \`cd W && make gate\` in the foreground (Bash timeout 600000). If it fails because of the rebase or step 1 (a spec_index Lines cell, name_residue, a doc check), fix it, \`git -C W commit --amend --no-edit\`, and re-run make gate; at most two fixes. A failure in code you did not touch: return failed with the gate's last lines. Never run a gate step by hand instead.
5. \`git -C M status --porcelain --untracked-files=no\` must print nothing; if it prints anything, return failed (do not touch M). Then \`git -C M merge --ff-only ${L.branch}\`. If it refuses because main moved (another lane merged), go back to step 3; at most three loops. Retry once on an index.lock error.
6. If the commit added a file under app/Sources (\`git -C M show --stat --diff-filter=A HEAD\`): \`cd M && make project\`.
7. From M: \`gh issue close ${it.n} --comment "<text>"\`: "Fixed in <short sha> (main, not pushed): <one-sentence what changed>. Verified: <short list>; make gate PASS." Mention any owed item.
8. Append one line to ${LOG}: "<date> <sha> lane-${L.lane} #${it.n} <subject>".
Never push, never force, never touch another worktree. Return the merged short sha.`,
    opts('integrate', { agentType: 'general-purpose', schema: INTEGRATE })))
  if (!integ) return { n: it.n, status: 'failed', detail: 'integrator returned nothing' }
  if (integ.status !== 'merged') return { n: it.n, status: integ.status, detail: integ.detail }
  log(`${tag} merged to main as ${integ.sha}`)
  return { n: it.n, status: 'merged', sha: integ.sha, detail: integ.detail }
